  "body": "Zstandard doesn't escape the tidal wave of bug hunting currently sweeping the industry.\r\nThis release comes mid-way through an effort that was initially meant to bring you the next version of Zstandard. Instead, it was refocused on answering the avalanche of reports received in the past few weeks. Thankfully, most of them are minor (or duplicates), but one of them is going to be published as a CVE, and that is why we are publishing this early release today.\r\n\r\nWe'll continue working on the initially intended scope of Zstandard v1.6.x in the coming weeks. In the meantime, updating to v1.6.0 is highly recommended.\r\n\r\n_edit_: CVE published, this is [CVE-2026-124851](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-124851)\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n- fix: streaming decompression of malformed data could expose uninitialized memory (#5023)\r\n- fix: multithreaded compression with `ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix()` could rarely emit a valid frame encoding wrong data, depending on thread timing (#5012)\r\n- fix: out-of-bounds read and write in the DDict hash table when using `ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts` (#4731)\r\n- fix: use-after-free of a `ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix()` prefix after `ZSTD_DCtx_reset()` following a malformed frame header (#4848)\r\n- fix: out-of-bounds read with `ZSTD_c_stableInBuffer` after an abandoned frame or a changed input buffer, reported by @IlyaGrebnov (#4943)\r\n- fix: multithreaded compression use-after-free when freeing or resetting a context during an abandoned frame (#4871)\r\n- fix: multithreaded streaming compression accepted a wrong pledged source size, producing corrupted frames (#4931)\r\n- fix: prepared dictionary decompression now rejects matches into formatted dictionary headers (#4991)\r\n- fix: on a static DCtx, `ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary()` and `ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix()` return `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` for nonempty dictionaries (#4914)\r\n- fix: wild reads when compressing with large dictionaries whose repcodes point into discarded content (#4915)\r\n- fix: memory corruption in `ZSTD_compressSequences()` and `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals()` with small `dst`, overflowing lengths, or some invalid sequences (#4918, #4989, #5004)\r\n- fix: out-of-bounds write with `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize` and `ZSTD_compress2()` into a `dst` smaller than `ZSTD_compressBound()` (#4981)\r\n- fix: high compression levels read uninitialized statistics with some dictionaries (#4978)\r\n- fix: 32-bit multithreaded compression with large windows (#4946, #4948)\r\n- fix: 32-bit builds rejected valid dictionary IDs above 4294967176 (#4976)\r\n- fix: excessive memory usage with long distance matching and small windows (#4626)\r\n- fix: CDict and DDict creation and size estimation reject dictionary sizes that overflow (#4912)\r\n- fix: crash when a custom allocator fails (#4613), data race when resizing a thread pool (#4601)\r\n- fix: legacy decoders: out-of-bounds reads, wrong streaming output, and offset validation (#4555, #4815, #4816, #4817, #4913, #4955, #4957)\r\n- api: legacy format support is now disabled by default (#4554)\r\n- api: experimental `ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts` requires an exact dictionary ID match: a missing nonzero ID returns `ZSTD_error_dictionary_wrong` instead of falling back to the current dictionary (#4929)\r\n- api: disabling experimental `ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts` releases every dictionary reference of its set (#4929)\r\n- api: removed the deprecated experimental functions `ZSTD_copyCCtx()` and `ZSTD_copyDCtx()` (#4960)\r\n- api: promoted `ZSTD_getFrameHeader()` and `ZSTD_FrameHeader` to the stable API (#2471)\r\n- api: promoted `ZSTD_createDDict_byReference()`, `ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary_advanced()`, and `ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary_advanced()` to the stable API, along with `ZSTD_dictContentType_e` and `ZSTD_dictLoadMethod_e` (#4283, #3723)\r\n- api: `ZSTD_decompressDCtx()`, `ZSTD_decompress_usingDict()` and `ZSTD_decompress_usingDDict()` reset an unfinished streaming session, as documented (#4975)\r\n- api: `ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary()` returns `ZSTD_error_dictionary_corrupted` for a corrupted dictionary, instead of `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` (#4925)\r\n- api: `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals()` enforces its documented limits on block size and `litBufCapacity` (#4741, #4782)\r\n- api: `ZSTD_decompressContinue()` returns `ZSTD_error_stage_wrong` when not preceded by `ZSTD_decompressBegin()` (#4937)\r\n- api: new experimental `ZSTD_isDeterministicBuild()` (#4331)\r\n- perf: faster decompression on AArch64 (#4413, #4414, #4418, #4509), by @arpadpanyik-arm\r\n- perf: faster compression on AArch64 with SVE2 (#4411), by @arpadpanyik-arm\r\n- perf: faster `ZSTD_compressSequencesAndLiterals()` on AArch64 with Neon and SVE2 (#4429, #4440), by @arpadpanyik-arm, and on RISC-V with RVV (#4399), by @zijianli1234\r\n- perf: faster row match finder on RISC-V with RVV (#4481), by @w1m024\r\n- cli: new `--patch-apply` command, equivalent to `-d --patch-from` (#4350)\r\n- cli: `-B#` renamed `--jobsize=#`, and benchmark `--blocksize=#` renamed `--split=#`; old names remain supported (#4329)\r\n- cli: `--filelist=` supports process substitution (#4349)\r\n- cli: size arguments accept `G`, `GB` and `GiB` suffixes (#4609), by @Integral-Tech\r\n- cli: `--memory=` also limits `.xz` and `.lzma` decompression (#4903)\r\n- cli: benchmark mode uses 1 thread by default (#4475)\r\n- cli: warn when multiple threads are requested for decompression (#4335)\r\n- cli: safer file handling: no output through symbolic links (#4906), `-r` no longer follows links and junctions on Windows (#4905), better same-file detection on Windows (#4884), robust to concurrent renames (#4962, #4999, #5003, #5009)\r\n- cli: `--output-dir-flat` fails on output filename collisions before processing (#4974), by @daniellerozenblit\r\n- cli: fix `zstd -l` infinite loop on a large skippable frame (#4833)\r\n- cli: fix `--memlimit-decompress=` parsing (#4916), `--adapt` bounds (#4982), `--patch-from` with an empty file (#4896), `--check` with `--format=lz4` (#5011)\r\n- cli: fix `ZSTD_NBTHREADS=0` (#4334), \r\n- cli: fix decode-only benchmark of multiple files (#4714, #4945)\r\n- cli: `zstdgrep` exits 0 when any of several files matches (#4967)\r\n- zdict: fix out-of-bounds reads with small training sets (#4690, #4710, #4922), and COVER results no longer depend on memory addresses (#4765)\r\n- contrib: seekable_format: fix out-of-bounds reads, infinite loops and error recovery on malformed seek tables (#4712, #4717, #4902, #4941, #4942, #4958)\r\n- contrib: zlibWrapper: no longer writes an empty gzip member after `Z_FINISH` (#4818)\r\n- build: `ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT` defaults to `0` in all build systems (#4554, #4781)\r\n- build: root `CMakeLists.txt` wrapper (#4491)\r\n- build: cmake: C++ only required for tests (#4357), ASM only enabled when needed (#4504), separate export groups (#4494), static API visibility applied to the shared library (#4789), Android build (#4447)\r\n- build: fix cmake with clang-cl (#4810, #4972), \r\n- build: fix meson on Windows (#4322), duplicate `LC_RPATH` on macOS 15.4+ (#4371), Swift module map (#4531), musl (#4336), OpenBSD and NetBSD (#4463)\r\n- build: meson calls `meson.override_dependency()` (#4472), by @bgilbert\r\n- build: Windows release binaries support lz4 (#4327), and new Windows ARM64 binaries (#4465)\r\n- portability: RISC-V 64-bit detection (#4525)\r\n- doc: clarified `Block_Maximum_Size` in the format specification",
